      "notes": "Pulse now retries a rate-limited model call with jitter inside a budget sized to the platform ceiling, then degrades to facts only, with 732 tests covering the ladder. It also has the clearest cost story of the five: caching takes 6,240 model calls a day down to 325, the before and after is labelled as modelled rather than metered, and a live spend counter now ships. Untrusted material is fenced as data at the prompt boundary and re-checked by a deterministic guard on every publish, and the guard fixture floors run offline in CI on every pull request. Pillar math: Product Judgment = avg(D1 great, D2 good, D7 good, R1 weak, S4 good, GEN3 great) = 7.5; System Design = avg(S1 great, S2 good, S3 weak, S5 good, S8 good) = 7.0; Evaluation = avg(E1 good, E2 weak, E3 good, E4 good, E5 good) = 6.4; Reliability & Ownership = avg(B1 great, B2 good, B3 good, B4 good, B5 good, SH3 good, SH10 good) = 7.43; Safety = avg(E3 good, SH1 great, SH9 good, SH10 good) = 7.75; Economics = avg(S1 great, GEN3 great) = 10.0; Communication = avg(D1 great, SH4 good, D5 great, SH5 good) = 8.5; UX/UI & Interaction = avg(S4 good) = 7.0; Collaboration & Stakeholders = avg(D5 great, SH5 good, CS1 great) = 9.0. Overall = round(mean of 9 non-null pillars (7.842) x 10) = 78. Collaboration & Stakeholders is null: no stakeholder question was graded this run, so it stays a visible gap rather than a guess.",
